Okay, I solved this myself and I am putting my answer here because it may help others!
I got to the stage that indicated dartR was fully installed, but I tried gl.drop.pop and it would not work.
and then I noticed this output!

Be aware that owing to CRAN requirements and compatibility reasons not all functions of the package may run after the basic installation, as some packages could still be missing. Hence for a most enjoyable experience we recommend to run the function  gl.install.vanilla.dartR() This installs all missing and required packages for your version of dartR. In case something fails during installation please refer to this tutorial: https://github.com/green-striped-gecko/dartR/wiki/Installation-tutorial.
So I ran
gl.install.vanilla.dartR()
And lo and behold, I could do the things I wanted to do;
such as drop pops and keep individuals.

gl.plot(testset.gl <http://testset.gl>) ## to test the installation! still would not work.

Hope this helps someone.
Ruth

